# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*
# ...but the template carries no secrets and documents what keys are needed
!.env.example

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Strategy docs — deliberately NOT published.
#
# The GitHub repo is public. These three name a local competitor (with their
# phone number), carry a strategic assessment of them, and hold candid notes
# on the client's own gaps. This is a village where everyone knows everyone —
# the brief says so repeatedly — so none of it belongs in a searchable repo.
#
# They were also stripped from all 27 commits of history with filter-branch,
# because gitignoring alone would still have published every earlier copy.
# Full history is preserved locally on the `backup-full-history` branch.
#
# Keep them: they are the reason the build is the way it is. Just keep them
# here. CLAUDE.md is additionally rewritten by `next dev` on every run.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
CLAUDE.md
PLACEHOLDERS.md
RESEARCH_competitor_sites.md
